# Ring integration — required environment variables
#
# ⚠️ PUT THE VALUES IN THE REPO ROOT `.env`, NOT IN A COPY OF THIS FILE HERE.
#
# This file documents what Ring needs, because this package is where you will
# look for it. But every process in this repo loads ONE env file — the root
# `.env`, via `node --env-file-if-exists=.env` in the npm scripts. A second
# `.env` next to this file would be read by nothing and would cost you an
# afternoon working out why RING_HMAC_KEY was empty.
#
#   cd ~/projects/vouch
#   cp packages/ring-integration/.env.example - >> .env    # or just paste the
#                                                          # three lines below
#
# The root `.env` is gitignored. This example file is committed and must never
# hold a real value.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Credentials from the Ring Developer Portal
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Ring issues THREE things at partner onboarding, not two: a client id, a
# client secret, and a separate HMAC key. The HMAC key is the one that signs
# webhooks — using the client secret to verify a signature will fail, and it
# fails in the way that looks like Ring is sending bad signatures.

RING_CLIENT_ID=
RING_CLIENT_SECRET=

# Signs webhook deliveries. Verified as HMAC-SHA256 over the RAW request body,
# presented in the `X-Signature` header as `sha256=<hex digest>`.
#
# Re-serialising the parsed JSON before hashing will never match: key order
# and whitespace change, and the digest changes with them. Always hash the
# bytes as received.
RING_HMAC_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local capture (only needed while capturing a real payload)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Port `npm run ring:capture` listens on. It binds 0.0.0.0 so a tunnel can
# reach it.
# RING_CAPTURE_PORT=4100

# Where captured deliveries are appended, one JSON object per line.
# Defaults to packages/ring-integration/webhook-capture.jsonl, which is
# gitignored — captures contain real device ids and a real signature.
# RING_CAPTURE_FILE=
